{"content":[{"c":["SERVANT"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["A person under obligation to serve a master, who in turn would provide a measure of protection. Some servants were slaves under legal bondage; others were servants voluntarily. It is not always possible to distinguish among “servant,” “slave,” “bondman,” and “bondwoman.” Several words in both Hebrew and Greek have been translated “servant,” although newer translations sometimes prefer other words."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The Hebrew word for “lad,” “youth,” or “boy” often means servant (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.33.11","r":"Exod.33.11","rawR":"Exod.33.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.33.11","value":"Exod.33.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 33:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.22.22","r":"Num.22.22","rawR":"Num.22.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.22.22","value":"Num.22.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 22:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.4.12","r":"2Kgs.4.12","rawR":"2Kgs.4.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.4.12","value":"2Kgs.4.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 4:12"},"). A word meaning “free-born servant” referred to the servants of the Lord, like the Levites (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.17","r":"Ezra.8.17","rawR":"Ezra.8.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.17","value":"Ezra.8.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.61.6","r":"Isa.61.6","rawR":"Isa.61.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.61.6","value":"Isa.61.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 61:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.44.11","r":"Ezek.44.11","rawR":"Ezek.44.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.44.11","value":"Ezek.44.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 44:11"},") or priests (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.28.35","r":"Exod.28.35","rawR":"Exod.28.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.28.35","value":"Exod.28.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 28:35"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Joel.1.9","r":"Joel.1.9","rawR":"Joel.1.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Joel.1.9","value":"Joel.1.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jl 1:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Joel.2.17","r":"Joel.2.17","rawR":"Joel.2.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Joel.2.17","value":"Joel.2.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:17"},"). Sometimes ministers of the king are called servants (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.1","r":"1Chr.27.1","rawR":"1Chr.27.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.1","value":"1Chr.27.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Pr.29.12","r":"Pr.29.12","rawR":"Pr.29.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.29.12","value":"Pr.29.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 29:12"},"), as are angels who minister before the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.103.21","r":"Ps.103.21","rawR":"Ps.103.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.103.21","value":"Ps.103.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 103:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.104.4","r":"Ps.104.4","rawR":"Ps.104.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.104.4","value":"Ps.104.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"104:4"},"). The hired servant or hireling was also considered a free person (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.12.45","r":"Exod.12.45","rawR":"Exod.12.45","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.12.45","value":"Exod.12.45"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 12:45"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.7.1","r":"Job.7.1","rawR":"Job.7.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.7.1","value":"Job.7.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 7:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mal.3.5","r":"Mal.3.5","rawR":"Mal.3.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mal.3.5","value":"Mal.3.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mal 3:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["The most common Hebrew term, occurring nearly 800 times in the OT, denotes a slave held in bondage (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.9.25","r":"Gen.9.25","rawR":"Gen.9.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.9.25","value":"Gen.9.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 9:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.12.16","r":"Gen.12.16","rawR":"Gen.12.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.12.16","value":"Gen.12.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.20.17","r":"Exod.20.17","rawR":"Exod.20.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.20.17","value":"Exod.20.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 20:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.5.15","r":"Deut.5.15","rawR":"Deut.5.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.5.15","value":"Deut.5.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 5:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.15.17","r":"Deut.15.17","rawR":"Deut.15.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.15.17","value":"Deut.15.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:17"},"). Yet the same word is used for people of noble rank, such as ministers and advisers to the king (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.22.12","r":"2Kgs.22.12","rawR":"2Kgs.22.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.22.12","value":"2Kgs.22.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 22:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.34.20","r":"2Chr.34.20","rawR":"2Chr.34.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.34.20","value":"2Chr.34.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 34:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.2.10","r":"Neh.2.10","rawR":"Neh.2.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.2.10","value":"Neh.2.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 2:10"},") or a servant of God (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.24.14","r":"Gen.24.14","rawR":"Gen.24.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.24.14","value":"Gen.24.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 24:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.12.7","r":"Num.12.7","rawR":"Num.12.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.12.7","value":"Num.12.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 12:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.1.7","r":"Josh.1.7","rawR":"Josh.1.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.1.7","value":"Josh.1.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 1:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.21.8","r":"2Kgs.21.8","rawR":"2Kgs.21.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.21.8","value":"2Kgs.21.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 21:8"},"), in such expressions as “Moses [or also David, Isaiah, Israel, Job, etc.] my servant.” One of the noblest expressions is “the servant of Yahweh [the ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"divine-name","t":"span"},"]” (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.34.5","r":"Deut.34.5","rawR":"Deut.34.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.34.5","value":"Deut.34.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 34:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.1.13","r":"Josh.1.13","rawR":"Josh.1.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.1.13","value":"Josh.1.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 1:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.8.31-33","r":"Josh.8.31-33","rawR":"Josh.8.31-33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.8.31-33","value":"Josh.8.31-33"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:31-33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.49.1-6","r":"Isa.49.1-6","rawR":"Isa.49.1-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.49.1-6","value":"Isa.49.1-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 49:1-6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.50.4-9","r":"Isa.50.4-9","rawR":"Isa.50.4-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.50.4-9","value":"Isa.50.4-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"50:4-9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.52.13-53.12","r":"Isa.52.13-53.12","rawR":"Isa.52.13-53.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.52.13-53.12","value":"Isa.52.13-53.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"52:13–53:12"},"). The proper name Obadiah means “servant of Yahweh.”"],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["The NT variously defines servant as a hired servant or hireling (",{"href":"?bref=Mark.1.20","r":"Mark.1.20","rawR":"Mark.1.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.1.20","value":"Mark.1.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 1:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.15.17-19","r":"Luke.15.17-19","rawR":"Luke.15.17-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.15.17-19","value":"Luke.15.17-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 15:17-19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.10.12-14","r":"John.10.12-14","rawR":"John.10.12-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.10.12-14","value":"John.10.12-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 10:12-14"},"), more widely as a slave (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.8.9","r":"Matt.8.9","rawR":"Matt.8.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.8.9","value":"Matt.8.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 8:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.10.24-25","r":"Matt.10.24-25","rawR":"Matt.10.24-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.10.24-25","value":"Matt.10.24-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:24-25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.13.27-28","r":"Matt.13.27-28","rawR":"Matt.13.27-28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.13.27-28","value":"Matt.13.27-28"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:27-28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.10.44","r":"Mark.10.44","rawR":"Mark.10.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.10.44","value":"Mark.10.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 10:44"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.12.2-4","r":"Mark.12.2-4","rawR":"Mark.12.2-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.12.2-4","value":"Mark.12.2-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:2-4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.7.2-3,8-10","r":"Luke.7.2-3,8-10","rawR":"Luke.7.2-3,8-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.7.2-3,8-10","value":"Luke.7.2-3,8-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 7:2-3, 8-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.4.51","r":"John.4.51","rawR":"John.4.51","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.4.51","value":"John.4.51"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 4:51"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.8.34","r":"John.8.34","rawR":"John.8.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.8.34","value":"John.8.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.13.16","r":"John.13.16","rawR":"John.13.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.13.16","value":"John.13.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Eph.6.5","r":"Eph.6.5","rawR":"Eph.6.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eph.6.5","value":"Eph.6.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eph 6:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Col.1.7","r":"Col.1.7","rawR":"Col.1.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Col.1.7","value":"Col.1.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Col 1:7"},"), and also as a domestic servant (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.16.13","r":"Luke.16.13","rawR":"Luke.16.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.16.13","value":"Luke.16.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 16:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=SlaveSlavery_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"SlaveSlavery_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"SlaveSlavery_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Slave, Slavery"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Servant","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 33:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.33.11","rawQueryValue":"Exod.33.11","sourceRefExact":"Exod.33.11"},{"anchorText":"Nm 22:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.22.22","rawQueryValue":"Num.22.22","sourceRefExact":"Num.22.22"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 4:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.4.12","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.4.12","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.4.12"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 8:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExa